1) Executive summary (short narrative you can open with)
- Example (assumes $62K burn): “Horizon Media holds $1.2M in cash and generated $1.8M revenue last quarter (annualized ~$7.2M). At our current cash burn of $62K/month, we have ~19 months of runway. Over the next 12 months we will focus on margin expansion and scalable revenue growth via higher-margin product packaging, automation of delivery, and tighter cost discipline. Target outcomes: improve gross margin by 6–10 p.p., reduce operating burn by 10–25%, and increase recurring revenue share, improving operating leverage and valuation multiple.”
- If burn is $200K/month (6 months runway): change “~19 months” to “~6 months” and emphasize immediate cost reductions and short-term liquidity actions.

2) Key financial metrics to present (must include these in decks/updates)
- Cash balance and runway (explicit scenario analysis at current burn and after savings)
