- If net burn is ~200K/mo you are in a higher-risk position and must prioritize immediate cost saves + revenue stabilization to reach break-even quickly.

Priority levers to improve margins (organized by timeline)
1) Immediate / 0–3 months (fast, low complexity)
- Reprice new business and close renewals at +5–10% where possible. Expected impact: +$30–60K/mo if applied selectively to new/renewal pipeline.
- Freeze non-essential hiring and discretionary spend. Typical savings: $10–50K/mo depending on hiring plan.
- Vendor & media-buy renegotiation (consolidate vendors, ask for volume discounts). Typical savings: 5–10% of vendor spend — often $10–30K/mo.
- Pause or wind down low-margin projects/accounts. Quick wins: remove projects that are cash-negative.
- Shorten DSO / tighten collections (incentives for faster payment). Improves working capital and reduces short-term cash strain.

2) Medium / 3–9 months (moderate effort)
- Productize services (standard packages, retainers, performance pricing). Benefit: higher margins on repeatable work — aim for +5–15% gross margin uplift.
- Automation of campaign ops and reporting (RPA, templates). Reduce FTE hours for delivery — convert into capacity rather than hiring. Savings: 1–3 FTE equivalents ($8–40K/mo).
- Upsell/cross-sell existing clients (retainers, analytics products). 1–3 existing clients moved to retainer can add steady, higher-margin revenue.
- Move portion of ad buy to programmatic/self-serve for lower overhead and better margin.

3) Long-term / 9–18 months (strategic, larger returns)
- Build or partner on a self-serve/ad-tech platform to lower marginal cost of revenue growth.
- Expand into SaaS-like products or licensing content/tech for recurring high-margin revenue.
- Strategic partnerships and channel/distribution to scale without proportional ops increases.

Concrete scenario examples (illustrative)
Assume monthly revenue = $600K.

Scenario A — Base (burn = $62K)
- Current net burn = 62K → runway ≈ 19.4 months.
- Initiative package (price +5% on pipeline = +$30K; vendor savings = $20K; automation saves = $10K) → net improvement = +$60K/mo.
