Case A — current burn $62K:
- Current runway ≈ 19.4 months
- Quick wins: 20% OPEX cut → new burn ≈ $49.6K → runway ≈ 24.2 months
- Pricing/COGS improvement (raise margin -> net savings equivalent to lowering burn by $15K) → new burn ≈ $34.6K → runway ≈ 34.7 months

Case B — current burn $200K:
- Current runway = 6 months
- Quick wins (hiring freeze + vendor cuts = 20%): save $40K → new burn = $160K → runway = 7.5 months
- Add pricing & sales efficiency (increase contribution by $30K): new burn ≈ $130K → runway ≈ 9.2 months
- Combine with automation/COGS reductions over 12 months (additional $30K): new burn ≈ $100K → runway = 12 months

(These are illustrative — I’ll model exact dollar impacts when you confirm real OPEX/COGS.)

Suggested finance narrative (one-page / slide flow)
