High-level finance narrative (one paragraph you can use)
"Horizon Media enters this planning cycle with $1.2M cash and recent quarterly revenue of $1.8M. Our immediate goal is to secure runway and improve unit economics by prioritizing high-margin revenue, reducing controllable costs, and shifting toward scalable, recurring revenue models. Over the next 90 days we will (1) implement quick margin & cash-conservation wins, (2) launch pricing & packaging experiments, and (3) build a 3-scenario forecast (downside / base / upside) to support investment or fundraising decisions. These steps should materially improve cash flow and position us to scale efficiently."

Priority levers to improve margin and scalability (prioritized)
1. Increase gross margin (highest leverage)
   - Reprice high-volume/low-margin services; introduce value-based pricing for premium clients.
   - Remove or repackage lowest-margin offerings; promote high-margin bundles.
   - Negotiate supplier/vendor/third‑party costs; convert fixed fees to variable where possible.

2. Improve revenue quality & scalability
   - Move toward recurring revenue (subscriptions, retainers) and annual contracts to reduce churn and smooth cash flow.
   - Standardize and productize services to reduce delivery cost per sale (templates, playbooks, automation).
   - Upsell/cross-sell to existing customers (higher ROI than new customer acquisition).

3. Reduce controllable cash burn (quick wins)
   - Hiring freeze for non-critical roles; reassign internal resources to revenue-generating work.
   - Pause or re-evaluate low-impact marketing spend; shift to performance-based channels.
   - Renegotiate payment terms with vendors; extend payables and accelerate receivables (discount for early payment).

4. Improve operational efficiency
   - Automate repeatable tasks (reporting, billing, ad ops) to reduce headcount growth needs.
   - Outsource where variable pricing reduces fixed cost pressure.
   - Track utilization and revenue per employee to set hiring triggers.

5. Sales & GTM scalability
   - Build a self-serve / low-touch channel for smaller clients; use an enterprise motion for large accounts.
   - Introduce a customer success function to increase retention and expansion.
   - Partner/channel strategy to expand reach without linear sales costs.

Cash & financing actions to consider
- Short term: tighten DSO (collections), push for advance payments or deposits on large projects, consider short-term credit line or factoring if runway is tight.
- Medium term: prepare a fundraising or bridge plan (clear use of proceeds, runway extension scenarios).
- Maintain a 13-week rolling cash forecast and update weekly.

