- Optimize media/vendor buys: layer discounts, consolidated buys, performance guarantees.
- Centralize finance & procurement to enforce budget discipline.
- Introduce KPIs and incentives tied to gross margin and CAC payback.

Scalability levers (12+ months)
- Standardize onboarding and playbooks so each new client scales with sub-linear cost growth.
- Build a repeatable sales funnel with clear CAC, payback period, and LTV targets.
- Invest in platform/tech that enables self-serve or lower-touch delivery models for smaller clients.
- Move some fixed costs to variable (outsourcing, variable-rate vendors) where possible.

KPIs to include in the materials
- Monthly revenue, MRR/ARR equivalent, YoY and QoQ growth
- Gross margin % (by product line)
- Net burn (cash outflow − cash inflow)
- Runway (cash / net burn)
- CAC, LTV, LTV:CAC, CAC payback (months)
- Contribution margin per client / campaign
- Churn (revenue and customer)
- Burn multiple (net burn / net new ARR)

Simple scenario math (pick which baseline applies)
A. If burn = $62K/month:
- Implied monthly expenses = revenue + burn = $600K + $62K = $662K
- Runway = $1.2M / $62K ≈ 19.4 months
- Quick 10% cost reduction (≈ $66K/month) → new burn ≈ $62K − $66K = net positive cash (~$4K/month net inflow). Outcome: immediate cash-positive operations and runway effectively extended indefinitely if revenue holds.
B. If runway = 6 months → implied burn = $200K/month:
- Implied monthly expenses = revenue + burn = $600K + $200K = $800K
- Runway = $1.2M / $200K = 6 months
- Quick 10% cost reduction (≈ $80K/month) → new burn ≈ $120K/month → new runway = $1.2M / $120K = 10 months
- Combine with modest revenue lift (10% increase → +$60K/month revenue) → adjusted burn: expenses (still estimated) − new revenue = (previous expenses − cost reductions) − new revenue change → net burn could fall to ~60K/month → runway extends to ~20 months.

Suggested 90-day targets (examples to include in slides)
- Achieve $60–100K/month cost savings through vendor renegotiation and discretionary spend freeze.
- Launch 1 pricing/packaging change to lift gross margin by 3–7 p.p. within 60 days.
- Reduce AR days by 20% to increase near-term cash flow.
