Response (FULL, NOT TRUNCATED):
I can help — but first I need to clarify one key inconsistency so the numbers and narrative are accurate.

Quick check of the numbers you gave
- Cash = $1.2M
- Stated runway = 6 months → implies burn ≈ $1.2M / 6 = $200K/month
- You also wrote burn rate = $62K/month → implies runway ≈ $1.2M / $62K ≈ 19.4 months
- Revenue last quarter = $1.8M → monthly revenue ≈ $600K

Which of these is correct:
A) The runway is really 6 months (so burn ≈ $200K/mo), or
B) The burn rate is really ≈ $62K/mo (so runway ≈ 19 months), or
C) You meant something else (e.g., $62K is net burn after factoring some adjustments, or $1.2M is cash excluding restricted amounts)?

Please confirm which is accurate (or give the correct operating expense / cash burn number). Meanwhile, below are actionable recommendations you can use immediately for margin improvement, scalability and an internal finance narrative.

Immediate messaging / finance narrative (short version)
- Snapshot: Cash $1.2M; runway X months (clarify); last quarter revenue $1.8M (avg $600K/mo). Our priority is to extend runway while improving margins and preserving growth.
- Near-term goals (0–3 months): Stop non-essential spend, prioritize high-margin clients, tighten collections, and create a 12-month rolling cash forecast and three scenarios (base / downside / upside).
- Mid-term (3–9 months): Improve gross contribution by pricing/packaging changes, improve utilization/productization, and invest in automation that reduces per-unit delivery cost.
- Long-term (9–18 months): Scale through repeatable offerings, sales playbooks, and platform/tech investments that reduce marginal cost per additional revenue dollar.
- Ask of leadership: Approve a short-term cost-savings plan, prioritize a growth sprint targeting top 20% of clients (by margin), and greenlight a 12-month forecast/plan to present to the board.

Concrete levers to improve margin (ranked by speed to implement)
1. Pricing and packaging (fast, high impact)
   - Raise rates selectively for low-discount or high-value clients.
   - Introduce packaging (retainer, tiered services) that converts one-off work into recurring, higher-margin revenue.
   - Expected impact example: +5 percentage points margin on $1.8M/quarter = +$90K/quarter (~$30K/month).

2. Client profitability focus (fast)
   - Identify top/bottom 20% of clients by margin; double down on top, reduce or exit bottom.
   - Stop low-margin deals or increase prices/terms.

3. Increase utilization / productivity (medium)
   - For service teams: target higher billable utilization, reduce bench time.
   - Invest in templates/playbooks to reduce delivery time per project.

4. Cost rationalization (fast to medium)
   - Freeze non-essential hiring, renegotiate vendor contracts, defer capital projects.
   - Convert fixed costs to variable where possible (contractors, performance-based vendors).

5. Operational automation (medium)
   - Billing/collections automation to reduce DSO and shrink working capital needs.
   - Internal tooling to reduce delivery costs over time.

6. Productize & scale (longer-term)
   - Build repeatable offerings (SaaS modules, packaged services) that lower marginal cost per sale.
   - Standardize onboarding and pricing for easier scaling.

Scalability actions (process + organizational)
- Standardize repeatable sales motions and onboarding playbooks for faster ramp of new accounts.
- Build a tiered customer success model (self-serve + high-touch) to scale support cost-effectively.
- KPI-driven hiring: bring on managers/ops before expanding IC headcount.
- Invest in a small, high-leverage engineering/tooling capability to automate routine delivery tasks.

Financial modeling & analyses to include in materials
- 12-month rolling cash forecast (monthly) with three scenarios:
  - Base: current assumptions
  - Downside: revenue -15% and no savings
  - Recovery: revenue +20% with 10–20% margin improvement
- Sensitivity table showing impact to runway of:
  - X% reduction in costs
  - X% increase in prices / gross margin
  - Y% increase in revenue
- Unit economics / contribution margin by product or service line (revenue less directly attributable variable cost)
- Top 10 clients revenue vs. margin concentration and churn risk
- CAC / payback (if applicable) and LTV by client segment

Suggested KPIs to show on one slide
- Cash balance and runway (months) — main headline
- Monthly revenue (MRR if recurring) and QoQ growth
- Gross margin and contribution margin
- Operating expenses (OPEX) by fixed vs variable
- Net burn (cash outflow minus inflow) per month
- DSO / AR aging
- Top 10 customers % of revenue
- Utilization rate (if service business)
- New logo revenue and churn rate

Example scenarios (illustrative)
- If runway = 6 months (implied burn = $200K/mo): a 25% reduction in operating expense would cut burn to $150K/mo and extend runway from 6 → 8 months.
- If burn = $62K/mo (implied runway ≈ 19 months): focus more on scaling—prioritize investments that increase margin and lock in recurring revenue.

Prioritized 30/60/90 day plan
- 0–30 days: Confirm accurate cash and burn math, build monthly cash projection, halt non-essential spend, tighten AR.
- 31–60 days: Implement pricing changes for select clients, renegotiate top 5 vendor contracts, implement utilization targets.
- 61–90 days: Launch productization pilots, automate billing/collections, prepare revised 12-month plan for exec review.

What I can deliver for you next (pick one or more)
- I can draft the 1-page finance narrative / slide-ready bullet points and a one-slide summary (cash + runway + asks).
- I can build a 12-month cash and P&L model (spreadsheet-style) with scenario toggles.
- I can draft the internal email to leadership presenting the plan and asks.
- I can run the sensitivity examples with your confirmed burn number.

Next step
Please confirm the correct burn/runway figures (or give an operating expense breakdown / monthly P&L if available) and tell me which deliverable you want first (one-pager narrative, slide bullets, cash model, or internal email). I'll start producing it right away.

