  - Combining a 10% spend cut + 10% revenue growth → net burn ≈ $60K/month → runway ≈ 20 months

2) Margin improvement & scalability levers (with typical impact ranges)
- Gross margin / revenue-side
  - Pricing & packaging: +2–8 p.p. gross margin depending on elasticity. Quick wins by tightening discounting rules and annualizing contracts.
  - Upsell / cross-sell to top 20% customers: +5–15% revenue uplift in 3–6 months if pipeline exists.
  - Improve collections (reduce DSO by 10–20 days): immediate working capital release. Example: at $600K/month, one day ≈ $20K → 15 days ≈ $300K cash freed.
- Cost / margin-side
  - Personnel optimization: hiring freeze + reprioritize headcount can reduce burn 10–30% (depending on current people cost).
  - Cut discretionary spend (travel, events, contractors): 5–10% immediate expense reduction.
  - SaaS & vendor renegotiation: 10–30% on non-core subscriptions / services.
