Thanks — I can help. First, a quick clarification and a few baseline calculations, then recommended levers, a prioritized 30/60/90-day plan, and a short draft finance narrative you can use in internal materials.

Quick reconciliation (please confirm which is correct)
- You reported: cash = $1.2M, burn = $62K/month, runway = 6 months.
- Those three don’t line up mathematically:
  - If burn = $62K/mo, runway = $1,200,000 ÷ $62,000 ≈ 19.4 months.
  - If runway = 6 months, implied burn = $1,200,000 ÷ 6 = $200K/month.
- Revenue last quarter = $1.8M → average monthly revenue = $1.8M ÷ 3 = $600K/month.

Tell me which runway/burn number is accurate (or if you’re including forecasted headcount, one-time payments, or seasonality that raise expected future burn). I’ll use the correct one for precise cash-impact projections. Meanwhile I’ll give recommendations using the current revenue base ($600K/mo) and show how each lever moves cash.

Useful rule-of-thumb
- At $600K/mo revenue, each 1 percentage-point change in margin = $6,000/month (or $72,000/year). Use that to quickly translate margin improvements into dollars.

Priority levers to improve margin and scalability
(organized by speed-to-impact)

Quick wins (days → 30 days)
- Pricing / yield optimization
  - Test a 3–5% price increase where contracts allow or on new deals. A 5% uplift on $600K/mo = +$30K/mo.
  - Revisit discounting policy and approval thresholds.
- Collections & working capital
  - Reduce DSO by 10 days — converts receivables to cash and reduces financing need. If you run 60 days DSO on $600K/mo, a 10-day drop frees ~ $200K in working capital (approx).
- Immediate expense pruning
  - Freeze non‑critical hiring, halt discretionary spend, audit subscriptions. Target 5–10% SG&A reduction as a first step.
- Low-effort revenue lifts
  - Short-term upsells to top clients (priority outreach to top 10 clients for add-ons/specials).

Near-term actions (30 → 90 days)
- Productize and package higher-margin offerings
  - Create standardized media or analytics packages to increase gross margin and reduce delivery cost per dollar of revenue.
- Sales efficiency improvements
  - Reallocate seller time to higher ARPU verticals, shorten sales cycle, implement playbooks.
- Vendor renegotiations
  - Renegotiate ad tech, platform, and media supplier terms; seek volume or payment-term discounts.
- Outsource or automate non-core functions
  - Move lower-value work to lower-cost providers or automate repetitive ops.

Medium/long-term (90+ days)
- Diversify revenue streams
  - Subscription-based analytics, managed services, white-label products — aim for higher recurring revenue and predictable margins.
- Platform / tech investments that scale
  - Invest in automation that reduces delivery cost per campaign (e.g., automated reporting, programmatic optimizations).
- Strategic partnerships & channel sales
  - Partnerships that bring high-margin leads or co-sell opportunities.

Illustrative impact examples (order-of-magnitude)
- 5% price uplift → +$30K/mo → +$360K/yr.
- 3 percentage-point gross-margin improvement (through pricing + vendor savings) → 3 × $6K = +$18K/mo incremental margin on current revenue — note: that’s per percentage point of overall gross margin (multiply by the number of points).
- 10% SG&A cut (assume SG&A = $200K/mo as example) → $20K/mo saved. You can swap your real SG&A into this to model impact.
- Reducing DSO by 10 days at $600K/mo ≈ free up ~$200K working capital (one-time cash improvement).

KPIs to present in your materials (must-have)
- Cash on hand, burn rate, runway (explicit assumptions)
- Monthly/Quarterly revenue, revenue growth rate
- Gross margin and contribution margin (by product/service)
- DSO, AR (receivables), and billable utilization
- CAC, LTV (if relevant), churn by client cohort
- Revenue concentration (top 10 clients %)
- Pipeline coverage (expected bookings vs target)

30/60/90-day action plan (high level)
- 0–30 days
  - Reconcile cash/runway and prepare a 6–12 month cash forecast (daily/weekly updates).
  - Quick pricing experiments for new contracts; tighten discount approvals.
  - Freeze hiring, audit subscriptions, negotiate 30-day vendor reviews.
  - Outreach to top 10 clients to surface immediate upsell opportunities.
  - Owner: CFO + Head of Sales/Revenue Ops.
  - Target: reduce burn by X% (set specific % after you confirm SG&A).
- 31–60 days
  - Implement DSO reduction plan (incentives for early pay, shorter payment terms).
  - Negotiate vendor contracts, implement immediate saves.
  - Launch productized offerings pilot.
  - Owner: Head of Ops + Head of Product.
  - Target: +Y% margin improvement and Z weeks of runway extension.
- 61–90 days
  - Scale successful pilots, automate reporting/fulfillment processes to reduce delivery cost.
  - Finalize 12-month plan: revenue targets, cost baseline, hiring plan tied to revenue milestones.
  - Owner: CEO/CFO.
  - Deliverable: deck with scenario P&Ls (base, downside, upside).

Short finance narrative you can drop into a one-pager or slide
- Current state: “Horizon Media enters the quarter with $1.2M cash and quarterly revenue of $1.8M (≈$600K/month). Our current burn metric and runway assumptions require alignment — we will finalize a 6–12 month cash forecast with conservative revenue assumptions by [date].”
- Objective: “Extend runway to ≥12 months while improving margins and preserving growth. We will accomplish this via immediate yield and pricing actions, working-capital improvements, a targeted SG&A reduction program, and productization to increase recurring, higher-margin revenue.”
- Key actions & impact: (bullet three highest-impact items with estimated monthly cash effect)
  - “1) 5% effective price/yield lift → +$30K/month”
  - “2) Reduce DSO by 10 days → ~+$200K one-time cash”
  - “3) 10% SG&A reduction → (insert your SG&A-based $ savings)”
- Ask of leadership: “Approve immediate hiring freeze and pricing experiments, authorize vendor renegotiation, and commit functional leaders to 30/60/90-day targets. We will present a final 12-month plan with scenarios on [date].”

Slides / deliverables I can prepare for you
- 1-page executive summary (metrics, ask, topline actions + impact)
- 3-slide internal finance deck: Current state, Actions & timeline, Financial scenarios (base/downside/upside)
- Detailed 6–12 month cash-flow forecast and scenario modeling

Next steps for me
1) Tell me which burn/runway number is correct (is burn actually $62K or is runway limited to 6 months because of forecasted increases?). 2) If you want concrete numbers, upload or paste your latest P&L (monthly), balance sheet (cash & AR), and top 10 client revenue breakdown — I’ll build a 6–12 month forecast and produce the 1-page executive summary and 3-slide deck with modeled impacts.

Would you like me to draft the 1-page executive summary and a 3-slide deck now using the assumptions you confirm (burn = $62K or burn = $200K)? Which runway/burn should I assume?

